<figure class="companion-map" aria-labelledby="dns-map-title">
  <figcaption><span>Resolution map</span><h3 id="dns-map-title">A short name can produce several DNS queries</h3><p>The Pod's resolver applies its search rules first. Cluster DNS then answers a Kubernetes name or forwards another name upstream.</p></figcaption>
  <div class="lane"><span>Application</span><b>lookup “api”</b><i>→</i><b>Pod resolver</b><i>→</i><b>search suffixes</b></div>
  <div class="lane purple"><span>Cluster DNS</span><b>Service record?</b><i>→</i><b>Endpoint records?</b><i>→</i><b>cache response</b></div>
  <div class="lane green"><span>Answer</span><b>ClusterIP</b><em>or</em><b>Pod IPs</b><em>or</em><b>upstream result</b></div>
  <div class="map-foot">A DNS answer identifies an address. Service proxying or pod routing still has to deliver the connection.</div>
</figure>
